# Build context hygiene.
#
# Without this, `docker build` uploads node_modules and dist into the daemon on
# every build — hundreds of megabytes of files the image then rebuilds from
# scratch anyway, since the Dockerfile installs its own dependencies and
# compiles its own output.

# Dependencies and build output — the image produces both itself.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets must never enter a build context; a layer keeps them even if a later
# step deletes the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and CI
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# Tests, benchmarks, and tooling — not needed to build or run the image.
tests/
bench/
scripts/
vitest.config.ts
vitest.integration.config.ts
coverage/
*.lcov

# Documentation
*.md
LICENSE

# Container and orchestration files — never part of their own build context.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
nginx/

# Editor and OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
